TC 1–4
BDS 0,8: Aircraft identificationIdentification and category messages; typically callsign and emitter category.


TC 5–8
BDS 0,6: Surface positionPosition messages used when the aircraft is on the ground; incl. ground movement and track angle.


TC 9–18
BDS 0,5: Airborne positionThe most common airborne-position squitters with barometric altitude and CPR latitude/longitude fragments.


TC 19
BDS 0,9: Airborne velocityVelocity messages with ground speed, track, and vertical rate.


TC 20–22
BDS 0,5: Airborne position with GNSS altitudePosition messages using GNSS altitude.


TC 31
BDS 6,5: Operational statusADS-B version, integrity, capability, and status indicators.












Tip



Several type codes can map to the same BDS label. In that case, the type code is not just a message-family identifier: it also carries uncertainty information about the position or velocity encoded in the message.


The three demodulated ADS-B samples below correspond to the highlighted rows in the table: aircraft identification, airborne position, and airborne velocity. Each frame starts and ends with the usual Mode S envelope (DF/CA, aircraft address, and parity). The middle part is the ADS-B message field (ME), whose first five bits give the type code.

adsbTypeCode = (hex) =&gt; parseInt(hexToBits(hex.slice(8, 10)).slice(0, 5).join(""), 2)







adsbContent = (tc) =&gt; {
  if (tc &gt;= 1 && tc &lt;= 4) return "aircraft identification";
  if (tc &gt;= 5 && tc &lt;= 8) return "surface position";
  if (tc &gt;= 9 && tc &lt;= 18) return "airborne position with barometric altitude";
  if (tc === 19) return "airborne velocity";
  if (tc &gt;= 20 && tc &lt;= 22) return "airborne position with GNSS altitude";
  if (tc === 31) return "operational status";
  return "reserved or uncommon ADS-B content";
}







adsbDecodedPayload = (decoded, tc) =&gt; {
  const payload = {...decoded};
  if ((tc &gt;= 9 && tc &lt;= 18) || (tc &gt;= 20 && tc &lt;= 22)) {
    delete payload.latitude;
    delete payload.longitude;
    if (payload.lat_cpr !== undefined) {
      payload.cpr_lat = payload.lat_cpr;
      delete payload.lat_cpr;
    }
    if (payload.lon_cpr !== undefined) {
      payload.cpr_lon = payload.lon_cpr;
      delete payload.lon_cpr;
    }
  }
  return payload;
}







